  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Petco lit up early and never dimmed. A 7-0 shutout that felt decided by the end of the first inning.",
    "what_this_means": "Luis Campusano went 3-for-4 and drove in a run, but this was a team effort. They scored in four different innings, converted five of seventeen RISP situations, and the bullpen locked down completely. Matsui threw three scoreless, M\u00e1rquez five more of the same to earn the save. What looked like a chance to squander another close game became a game that wasn't close at all. The Padres got a lead early and held it flat through nine innings. The staff. Starter, bridge, closer. Did its job in lockstep. That matters because it's rare for them. A win this clean is rare for them.",
